digna@essex.ac.uk (Dignum A W) writes:

>   1) Is it true that you must take off all your armor before sitting 
>      on a throne? I read this in a fortune cookie so I know it may not be

No. There are two kind of fortunes in the fortune cookies, true ones and
bare rumors. This is the latter kind of fortune.
But I recommend you to drop your gold before sitting, since one possible
effect of sitting on the throne is losing all the gold you're carrying.

>   2) Is hell entirely composed of maze levels? If it is I could die of

There is also the tower, 3 levels high, in the middle of those levels.
You can only enter it from the lowest tower level, and there are ladders
between those levels inside the tower. 

>   3) Is it only possible to get into the rear section of the castle via
>      the back door? Is there a way through from the front?

Yes, if you can get the drawbridge down. Certain wands, spells or instruments
can do this.

>   4) Who the hell is Maud?

"Who the hell cares who that Maud person was, anyway.." :-)

